# Cloudflare production deploy

Production is **Cloudflare Containers**, and it is the only host. Vercel was fully removed on
2026-08-04 — do not reintroduce `vercel.json`, `.vercel/`, or any `vercel env pull` step.

- Live: `https://www.rillcod.com`, `https://rillcod.com`, `https://cf.rillcod.com`
- Auto-deploy: push to `main` → `.github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare.yml`
- Local deploy: `npm run deploy` (Docker required)
- Source of truth: `docs/CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md`

When changing deploy, DNS, crons, or hosting:

1. Read `docs/CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md` and `wrangler.toml` first.
2. Keep Containers + `Dockerfile.cf` + `scripts/cf-container-deploy.mjs`.
3. Do not switch production to another host without an explicit user request.
4. Do not remove GitHub Actions deploy secrets docs or the workflow without replacing them.
5. `wrangler.toml` must have **no** `[triggers]` block — cron-job.org owns scheduling, and a
   block here double-fires the reminder emails that go to parents.
6. Never sync a placeholder value (`[SENSITIVE]`, `changeme`) to Cloudflare — `npm run cf:env`
   rejects them, and bypassing that guard has already caused a production outage.
